  gear: { id: "gear", label: "Gear", rank: 5, template: `What the player character carries, wears and has to hand, and what of theirs is elsewhere, as it stands now: the authoritative list, one specific item a line. Name each item as given, with its details and condition, whenever the prose touches it; never replace it with a generic stand-in ("a bag", "some tools"). Having a thing isn't owning it: what they hold for someone, borrowed or took stays its owner's, as its line says, until the story has it given, sold or traded to them. A thing "Not with you" is somewhere else: they use it only once they have gone for it or had it brought.
{{lines}}`, position: { type: "chat_depth", role: "system", depth: 2, direction: "from_end" } },
