    text: `Put a place on a map, move it, rename it, say which map draws its inside, or take it off. A place put on a map is a new place of the world, inside the map's scope: its id must be one no place has yet. To put one, give map and name; to change one, name it in place and give what changes. Its description and other fields are not the map's: they can't be set here. Taking a place off the map takes it out of the world, with the map's links to it. Next: world_map_link joins the map's places. ${draft}`,
