    text: `Survey what there is to draw on before you prepare the story. Left without a part, it says what there is in outline: how long the chat is, how many summaries its World Info books hold at each level, its lore books, the world's people and places, and what the engine already holds. Each part then gives what it holds, in answers that fit (${at3("surveyChars")}): summaries, the story so far in the summaries' own text, the highest level first, then the lower levels newest first, with what was left out for size and how to read it; lore, each World Info book with its size and how many of its entries are always on, and with book, that book's entries; world, the world's people and places; engine, the clock, the cast, the beats and the minds; chat, the chat itself. It reads switched-off entries too, and reads only. On a chat with a history, read the summaries and the lore before you plan: the plan is refused until you have.`,
